{"year":"2026","sessionID":"2026GS","sessionIndex":"1","billNumber":"SB0207","billNumberShort":"S.B. 207","billNumberLong":"SB0207","fileNumber":"2026FL0770","shortTitle":"Protection from Unfair Treatment Based on Religion or Other Irrelevant Characteristics","currentSubVersion":"0","currentMinVersion":"0","primeSponsor":"BRAMMB","primeSponsorName":"Sen. Brammer, Brady","primeSponsorHouse":"S","floorSponsor":"TEUSCJ","floorSponsorName":"Rep. Teuscher, Jordan D.","floorSponsorHouse":"H","generalProvisions":"This bill prohibits, in relation to certain matters, unfair treatment based on a person's religion or other irrelevant characteristics.  ","highlightedProvisions":"This bill:<hr><ltbullet>defines terms;<hr><ltbullet>prohibits unfair treatment, by creditors or credit reporting agencies, based on a person's religion or other irrelevant characteristics;<hr><ltbullet>provides for administrative and legal enforcement of the provisions described in the preceding paragraph;<hr><ltbullet>prohibits unfair treatment by an insurer based on a person's religion or other irrelevant characteristics;<hr><ltbullet>provides for enforcement of the provisions described in the preceding paragraph;<hr><ltbullet>requires a local education agency to establish a policy granting an excused absence from school for a student to observe a religious holiday or attend religious instruction;<hr><ltbullet>requires a state institution of higher education to reasonably accommodate an individual's religious beliefs, faith, or conscience in relation to:<hr><ltbullet1>the state institution's admission process;<hr><ltbullet1>a student's attendance in class;<hr><ltbullet1>the scheduling of an examination or academic requirement; or<hr><ltbullet1>participation in a specific academic requirement; and<hr><ltbullet>makes technical and conforming changes.  ","moniesAppropriated":"None","draftingAttorney":"Thomas R. Vaughn","fiscalAnalyst":"Joseph Fitzgerald","lastAction":"Senate/ filed","lastActionOwner":"Se